  "description": "GEZJOM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H88 Dy8 N52 O10. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.674-4.132 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.43-124.60°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy8(bpt)8(μ4-O)2(μ-OMe)8(μ1,1,3,3-N3)(μ1,3-N3)(N3)2]·11H2O·9MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
